course: dictionary
lesson: 14667
title: Too early, too soon
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Prematurely is an adverb, and it means too early or before the proper time. Look at the word parts: «pre-» means before, and «mature» means fully grown or ready. So prematurely means before the right time. «The baby was born prematurely, so she needed special care in hospital.» The baby came early, before the usual time, so prematurely means too early.
explain: The word can also mean before you are ready or have the facts. «Don't celebrate prematurely; the final score is not in yet.» Cheering before the result is known is celebrating too soon. Ask yourself: what would happen if you did it too early? That question often reveals the meaning.
explain: Prematurely can describe things other than babies. «The leaves fell prematurely after the dry summer.» The leaves dropped before their usual time in autumn. «Grandad is prematurely grey» means his hair turned grey earlier than most people's does.
fact: Prematurely means too early, or before the usual or proper time.
fact: Prematurely is an adverb, so it tells you how or when something happens.
fact: The word is built from «pre-», meaning before, and «mature», meaning ready or fully grown.
fact: «Born prematurely» describes a baby who arrives before the usual time.
fact: «Celebrate prematurely» means cheering before you have enough facts or are ready.
exercise: «The baby was born prematurely.» What does prematurely mean here? | Happily | Very slowly | At the usual time | *Too early
exercise: «Don't celebrate prematurely.» What is the warning? | Cheer as loudly as you can | Dance on the way home | Celebrate at the very end of the match | *Do not cheer before you know the result
exercise: Ella's dad has grey hair at thirty. The writer says he is «prematurely grey». What does this mean? | Dyed his hair bright blue | *Went grey earlier than usual | Had his hair cut very short | Grew a very long beard
test: «The storm ended the game prematurely.» What does this tell you about the game? | It was finished exactly on time | It was started again | It lasted longer than usual | *It stopped before it should have
test: Sam shouted that he had won before the results were read out. Why was this a mistake? | He had already lost the game | Shouting is always wrong | The results were read out at the start | *He celebrated before he had the facts
exam: «The leaves fell prematurely in the dry summer.» Which answer best explains prematurely? | Very loudly in the wind | *Too early, before their usual time | Slowly and gently | After the autumn was over
